{
  "requirement": "The SDK formats node inputs using `NodeContents::format_node_content`,\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.fingerprinting.fingerprint_content`:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Method on NodeContents. Both arguments describe the already-read snapshot.\n/// Present these supplied contents as text for an agent.\nfn format_node_content(\n    &self,\n    node: &Self::NodeId,\n    contents: &Self::NodeContent,\n) -> Result<String, Self::Error>;\n```\n\nThe formatter uses the supplied contents; their fingerprint describes the same\nread. For inputs queued on an ask builder, formatting errors return\n`ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node` tool call, a formatting error is\nreturned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue and recover.\n`NodeContent` and `NodeId` retain their application-defined types without\nserialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation of `judge.rendering`. I did not request implementation source.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that check them**\n\n1. **Queued inputs are formatted with `NodeContents::format_node_content`.**\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` queues the current node, then successors, then the current node again. It asserts the rendered inputs reach the agent in the queued order, with repeats.\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` checks that the user message carries the rendered text.\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` checks that the domain's contents appear in the message in order.\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[validator_agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces]` sets `graph.formatter = distinct_pages`, so the output is distinguishable from the raw contents.\n\n2. **The formatter uses the supplied contents, so the text and fingerprint describe the same read.**\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` changes the underlying node after the snapshot is read. Formatting the snapshot still returns \"before\", and the fingerprint still matches the snapshot. Reads stay at `[1]`.\n   - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` formats a node that does not exist on disk. The output contains the supplied text and path, which shows the formatter does not re-resolve the node.\n   - The read counts in the explicit-insertion test, `[1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`, show one read per queued input and no rereads during formatting.\n\n3. **A formatting error on a queued input returns `ValidationError::Graph`.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` sets `fail_format` and asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded and that the agent request count is unchanged.\n\n4. **A formatting error during a `read_node` tool call is returned to the agent as a tool error so it can recover.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[node_rendering_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` uses a failing formatter. It asserts that the second request carries a `ToolResult` with `is_error`, the name `read_node`, and the error text. It then asserts that the agent submits successfully, so the call was not aborted. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded.\n\n5. **`NodeContent` and `NodeId` keep their application-defined types, with no serialization or display bounds.** The `Node` type in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` is documented as having no Serde or Hash implementations and derives only `Clone`, `Eq` and `PartialEq`. It has no `Display` or `Serialize`, and the agent tests compile and run with it. That serves as a compile-time check of the no-bounds obligation.\n\n**Gaps**\n\nNo gaps found. The acknowledgments list is empty, and none is needed.",
